condensed/b82bf69b-9432-4e48-aaf0-726a93740f62.md:811:  "summary": "Investigated gmMainLib_8015EA80 but found no source variant that improves on the existing 93.62857% checkpoint. The reference uses one persistent r30 base for every handicap store and retains otherwise-dead r31 plus r30 saves. The current helper shape instead creates four pointer webs for the two six-record groups, allocated to volatile registers. Direct natural-loop and typed-overlay variants collapse the stores to one base but eliminate the required stack frame and nonvolatile saves. I tested typed VsModeData helpers, direct for/do-while loops, pointer arrays, typed struct and union overlays, helper-boundary variants, counter types, and local-array hypotheses; all were no-ops or regressions. Two bounded source-permuter searches, including one from the structurally different direct-loop form, found no improvement. All experimental edits were reverted.",
condensed/b82bf69b-9432-4e48-aaf0-726a93740f62.md:815:  "match_percent": 93.62857,
condensed/b82bf69b-9432-4e48-aaf0-726a93740f62.md:817:    "checkdiff_run gmMainLib_8015EA80 --full-diff: FAIL at the restored 93.62857% baseline",
condensed/b82bf69b-9432-4e48-aaf0-726a93740f62.md:818:    "git diff -- src/melee/gm/gmmain_lib.c: clean; no retained edits",
condensed/b82bf69b-9432-4e48-aaf0-726a93740f62.md:821:  "allocator_evidence": "The restored helper shape produces base webs v33/v35 and v32/v34, colored to r5/r3 and r6/r4 respectively. The reference instead keeps all 72 stores relative to r30. Direct-loop variants produce the desired single-base displacement form but remove the 0xC8 frame and r30/r31 save/restore sequence, confirming a structural local maximum rather than a simple declaration-order issue.",
condensed/b82bf69b-9432-4e48-aaf0-726a93740f62.md:829:TOOL bash {"command":"git status --short && git diff -- src/melee/gm/gmmain_lib.c && sed -n '650,850p' src/melee/gm/gmmain_lib.c","timeout":20}
